      "content": "As you step out, the shadows seem to swallow whole figures that move with a predatory stillness, their eyes scanning the street with a calculated, predatory hunger that cuts deeper than any threat. You see street traders with disheveled faces selling too much polish for their scuffed boots, while hooded teens lock electric knives under their coats and whisper about street racers without looking directly at you. Every corner feels like a staging ground for a desperate game, where offers of free meals or warm jackets are the first thing you will see so you don't get spotted by the uncles who always watch and judge from their fire escapes.",
